  "course_description": "Investigation of a particular issue or topic in the study of language, linguistics, and communication. May be repeated when topic varies. Topics may include: the Romance languages; intercultural communication; words and the world; language and human nature.",
  "course_notes": "What happens when language development doesn't follow the expected path - or when the ability to use language is disrupted? Language Disorders provides an introduction to language disorders across the lifespan, from childhood developmental language difficulties to acquired disorders in adulthood. We'll explore how language disorders can affect speaking, listening, reading, writing, and everyday communication, while considering their linguistic, cognitive, neurological, and social foundations. Through real-world examples and clinical cases, students will learn how language disorders are identified, assessed, and treated. This course is especially relevant for students interested in linguistics, speech-language pathology, psychology, education, neuroscience, or anyone curious about the many ways language can develop and change.",
